  "answer": "I'll start by reading the project engineering notes and locating how special prices with dates are applied on the storefront API.The discount check looks wrong when a special has an end date. I'll trace how those dates are stored and how the storefront decides the price.A special price that included an end date never reached the storefront as a discount. The product-create mapper wrote that end date into the start-date field, and the price calculation then compared the start date with today a second time instead of checking that the end date was still in the future. Both are fixed: `PersistableProductAvailabilityMapper` now stores the end date on the end-date field, and `ProductPriceUtils` applies the special only while the end date is still ahead.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"No unit or storefront test covers a special price that has an end date, with or without a start date.\"], \"missing\": [\"A focused test that creates a product with a discounted price and an end date, then reads it back through the storefront price calculation.\"]}",
